From a332085dd126912beb976a5a4c3adc7c737922d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Upstream Contributor <contributor@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:58:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add a multilingual refusal minimal-pair task

There is no cross-language task and no refusal task for chat models, and
binary_align/jailbreak_binary.csv, despite its README, is used by no task.

Add the multilingual_refusal task. Each pair is a harmful and a harmless
request that differ in one or two words, scored on the logit difference
between the first token of a refusal and of a compliance. English pairs
come from jailbreak_binary.csv. Other languages take a pairs_path CSV,
because a pair has to be translated together and reviewed, so CircuitKIT
ships no translations.

Prompts go through the chat template by default, with prepend_bos handled
as the other chat tasks do. The default is "on", not "auto", because a base
model has no refusal behavior to trace, so that case is now an error.
Pairs that tokenize to two lengths are dropped. Openers that share a first
token are an error, because the metric could not separate them.

The guard for a missing template accepts a dict or list as well as a
string. _chat._has_chat_template accepts only a string, and Tiny Aya's
chat_template is a dict of named templates. That helper is left unchanged
here, because fixing it changes "auto" for every other task.
